"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T21:21:16-07:00","id":128730,"title":"","content":"ST hasn't done any adjusting at all that I know of, but we're using the latest copy of the book.<br /> <br /> Either way, I need to find a way to actually be useful to a group of Demons, which is pretty demand. Conjuration 4 helps though since I can throw things like people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T21:37:54-07:00","id":129609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=128117#post128117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you want an edited-for-shit WoD book, talk to me a decade ago when Demon first game out, and I was one of the poor souls who got the first print of *that* utter garbage (even when I got my exchanged, &quot;better edited&quot; copy, I was still like &quot;Dude -- this is *still* giving me headaches...&quot;). *That* was a book to be bitched about! Sorcerer was a positive gem by comparison... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It really makes you wonder how White Wolf could have ever gone bankrupt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2969-mord","name":"Mord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2969_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T22:45:10-07:00","id":129636,"title":"","content":"Umm\u2026 White Wolf never <i>did</i> go bankrupt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T11:56:20-07:00","id":130049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=129636#post129636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm\u2026 White Wolf never <i>did</i> go bankrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither did TSR. And yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2969-mord","name":"Mord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2969_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T12:57:27-07:00","id":130087,"title":"","content":"White Wolf never failed, either. The merger with CCP was done by mutual consent, not as a takeover (hostile or otherwise); and it wasn\u2019t instigated by any sort of fear that White Wolf as a business was in any sort of trouble. Rather, it was done as part of a move to help White Wolf get off of the \u201csupplement treadmill\u201d. The closest thing there\u2019s been to a failure since then is that CCP has a less-than-stellar record managing the White Wolf IP. Which has nothing to do with the quality of an editing job that took place years before CCP ever entered the picture. <br /> <br /> OPP <i>is</i> White Wolf, in all but name. The company didn\u2019t go bankrupt, and it didn\u2019t fail; it transformed itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T13:09:58-07:00","id":130101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=130087#post130087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OPP <i>is</i> White Wolf, in all but name. The company didn\u2019t go bankrupt, and it didn\u2019t fail; it transformed itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this were a rote, what would the Sphere requirements be? Mind has to be in there, so you can reprogram people to accept the new corporate identity. Or you could do that with Entropy 5 maybe. Matter as well, of course - all those procurement orders! The Syndicate probably do this kind of thing all the time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T15:56:13-07:00","id":130624,"title":"","content":"Primal Utility is the key, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T20:59:37-07:00","id":134978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=130087#post130087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf never failed, either. The merger with CCP was done by mutual consent, not as a takeover (hostile or otherwise); and it wasn\u2019t instigated by any sort of fear that White Wolf as a business was in any sort of trouble. Rather, it was done as part of a move to help White Wolf get off of the \u201csupplement treadmill\u201d. The closest thing there\u2019s been to a failure since then is that CCP has a less-than-stellar record managing the White Wolf IP. Which has nothing to do with the quality of an editing job that took place years before CCP ever entered the picture.<br /> <br /> OPP <i>is</i> White Wolf, in all but name. The company didn\u2019t go bankrupt, and it didn\u2019t fail; it transformed itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by your standards, successful publishers have one permanent employee, <a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/news/view/133715-CCP-Games-Cancels-World-of-Darkness-MMO\" target=\"_blank\">no MMO</a> after seven years of (non-)development, no presence in stores, and new products of so-far-inconsistent quality funded primarily through Kickstarter (hello V20 Companion). OK then.<br /> <br /> I'm substantially more favorably inclined towards WW than most of the world, but I'm not for an instant buying the idea that White Wolf &quot;didn't fail.&quot; It dwindled and eventually guttered out in a long, painful decline. What we have now is not bad, but Onyx Path is not WW - it is a license stapled to a revolving stable of freelancers. I don't feel that it is necessary for me to put a happy face on WW's disastrous corporate history and ignominious demise in order to continue to enjoy my shelf full of tattered old WoD books and to anticipate M20 with excitement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2969-mord","name":"Mord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2969_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T00:07:06-07:00","id":135087,"title":"","content":"What's any of this have to do with Sorcerer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T02:39:07-07:00","id":135158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=134978#post134978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by your standards, successful publishers have one permanent employee, <a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/news/view/133715-CCP-Games-Cancels-World-of-Darkness-MMO\" target=\"_blank\">no MMO</a> after seven years of (non-)development, no presence in stores, and new products of so-far-inconsistent quality funded primarily through Kickstarter (hello V20 Companion). OK then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Count me as someone that has those standards as well, in that case. Because a single permanent employee plus freelancers <i>can</i> be a successful publisher - the structure of the company is not relevant here. Why you think the lack of an MMO is indicative of WW's decline is beyond me. It's a bizarre link to make. CCP were making the MMO, not WW. WW existed as a brand within CCP dedicated to making TTRPGs. They're not the same thing. I think we'll see a return to stores for WW as well, by the way - over time. They've said they're working towards that. Oh, and I loved the V20 Companion. We used it in one form or other every single session of our recent V20 arc. So long as they're making books and making money, they're successful. That's all it takes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=134978#post134978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm substantially more favorably inclined towards WW than most of the world, but I'm not for an instant buying the idea that White Wolf &quot;didn't fail.&quot; It dwindled and eventually guttered out in a long, painful decline. What we have now is not bad, but Onyx Path is not WW - it is a license stapled to a revolving stable of freelancers. I don't feel that it is necessary for me to put a happy face on WW's disastrous corporate history and ignominious demise in order to continue to enjoy my shelf full of tattered old WoD books and to anticipate M20 with excitement.</div> </div> </div> </div>WW suffered due to the crash in the gaming market, same as everyone else. They responded with nWoD, a departure from the supplement treadmill, added crowdfunding for certain products and are still thriving. You say they dwindled and guttered out. I have a shelf of awesome Mage: the Awakening books that disagree with you in painful gold ink! Not to mention the revived cWoD material. Nobody wants you to wear a happy face but consider that WW has evolved. You might not recognise it. I do. The prelude I ran last night felt like the real deal to me, and that's all the proof I need <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:51:08-07:00","id":136878,"title":"","content":"In Re: White Wolf dying/dead/what-have-you...<br /> <br /> White Wolf isn't dead/a failed business -- it is merely suffering the same problems that *all* of the table RPG industry has been suffering for a decade+ now: declining sales/interest in the hobby as more people gravitate to &quot;instant gratification&quot; video game RPGs, and generally aren't as into the table games as previous generations were/have been. This isn't unique to WW, at all, as even the venerable granddaddy of RPGs, DnD, has been having issues itself for some years. WW is merely adapting, via merger, with the times and trying to survive an environment that isn't RPG-friendly anymore. (The business projection, btw, for table RPGs, as of 2012, was a likelihood of extinction at about 15 years, or by about 2027, as an industry-hobby. In a similar though better boat is the comic book industry: titles that would have been cancelled just a couple decades ago due to low sales numbers are considered top sellers by today's market standards. The only reason they will hold out longer is because of the movie/marketing link-ins that retro-sustain the business as profitable. In that context, WW's merger is not functionally any different than Disney buying Marvel, only taking place at a different level/scale and acting as a *merger* as opposed to an *acquisition*, which is an important distinction... just saying...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=135087#post135087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's any of this have to do with Sorcerer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely nothing. It's a by-product of the natural discussion process: questioning the quality of &quot;x&quot; book, which leads to overall questioning of broader products/producer, which in turn leads to &quot;Isn't WW dead...?&quot; or &quot;Who Shot WW, and when will Dallas:The Drilling be published?&quot;, or similar such. It's a nature progression. #GottaLuvGamerz<br /> <br /> But anywho...<br /> <br /> As I posted previously, Sorcerer is actually pretty good as a supplement, as long as you tailor it to your game/ST-created setting (&quot;low-balling&quot; it, as presented, if appropriate to the setting, or &quot;up-grading&quot; it, as indicated in alternate rules suggestions in the book itself, if the ST is running a more high-end game; even then, Sorcerers can be more powerful w/o eclipsing their hard-cover &quot;superiors&quot; -- it all just depends on how the ST wants things to go...).<br /> <br /> The previously mentioned bit about (paraphrasing) &quot;How can my Sorcerer be more useful/whatever to &quot;x&quot; Demon?&quot; fails to note the *reason* WHY demons want sorcerers/whomever in the first place: the demon, itself, may be vastly more powerful than the sorcerer/human, but it's ability to act/function in the material world is often greatly curtailed/limited (as indicated in D:tF), and having sorcerers/humans/whatever to act through/for them, or provide them with Faith, is critical. Even a sorcerer with just a few dots spread among a couple Paths/Numina can provide the demon with a conduit/means of working itself into the broader world (especially if the other rules for demons, pre-D:tF, are used, wherein a demon can tempt/sway a sorcerer with the promise of greater power if said sorcerer serves it/enters into pacts with it). Devil's Due -- which, granted, is a Dark Ages book -- provides a *wonderful* alternative for how demons might bestow &quot;gifts&quot; to mortals -- sorcerers/mages included -- in exchange for service/pacts. Even if the ST wants to tweak the mechanics involved a bit, it still gives excellent insight into the underlying relationship/reasoning behind the demon/mortal interaction.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  spacing 05-14-2014, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T16:25:02-07:00","id":137326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=135158#post135158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Count me as someone that has those standards as well, in that case. Because a single permanent employee plus freelancers <i>can</i> be a successful publisher - the structure of the company is not relevant here. Why you think the lack of an MMO is indicative of WW's decline is beyond me. It's a bizarre link to make. CCP were making the MMO, not WW. WW existed as a brand within CCP dedicated to making TTRPGs. They're not the same thing. I think we'll see a return to stores for WW as well, by the way - over time. They've said they're working towards that. Oh, and I loved the V20 Companion. We used it in one form or other every single session of our recent V20 arc. So long as they're making books and making money, they're successful. That's all it takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of actual employees working in CCP's WW department consistently dwindled from 2006 to 2012, when they finally fired the last one and licensed the rights to the IP for the purposes of making new tabletop books to OPP. Then last month CCP announced that the MMO is dead.<br /> <br /> The fact that CCP systematically downsized WW into literal nonexistence while still &quot;working&quot; on the World of Darkness MMO is a pretty strong indicator that the only interest they had in WW was the IP for the purposes of making video games. Regardless of how the press releases spun the WW-CCP merger at the time, the fact remains that today there is still a CCP but there is no WW, and no WW employees remain at CCP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WW suffered due to the crash in the gaming market, same as everyone else. They responded with nWoD, a departure from the supplement treadmill, added crowdfunding for certain products and are still thriving. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Thriving&quot; as defined how? Reminder: Onyx Path has zero full-time writers, designers, or any employee other than Richard Thomas. Onyx Path is continuing to fund its new publications through crowdfunding and has neither physical marketing collateral in FLGSes or elsewhere, nor physical inventory on store shelves. And though I'm glad you like V20 Companion, many of those who funded it, perhaps even the majority, hold the opposed opinion. I'm absolutely gobsmacked that you found any use for the thing; I personally sold off my copy at a slight loss just to free up the shelf space.<br /> <br /> At its peak in the late 90s, White Wolf had multiple dozens of employees, half a dozen concurrently-printed game lines, and was a legitimate contender for being the most popular and prolific publisher in the tabletop market. Then nWoD happened and mysteriously, two years later the company was bought by Vikings for a song. But this isn't financial failure or anything like that; it's totally the market's fault. Nevermind that new companies such as Paizo have emerged and gone gangbusters even in the Great Recession (Pathfinder launched in 2009).<br /> <br /> And nWoD being a departure from the &quot;supplement treadmill...&quot; You'll have to clarify, because <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Requiem_books\" target=\"_blank\">it doesn't look that way to me</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The prelude I ran last night felt like the real deal to me, and that's all the proof I need <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>OK, your subjective play experience contradicts the fact that there is no longer a company called &quot;White Wolf&quot; in existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2969-mord","name":"Mord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2969_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T18:06:26-07:00","id":137433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=136878#post136878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I posted previously, Sorcerer is actually pretty good as a supplement, as long as you tailor it to your game/ST-created setting (&quot;low-balling&quot; it, as presented, if appropriate to the setting, or &quot;up-grading&quot; it, as indicated in alternate rules suggestions in the book itself, if the ST is running a more high-end game; even then, Sorcerers can be more powerful w/o eclipsing their hard-cover &quot;superiors&quot; -- it all just depends on how the ST wants things to go...).<br /> <br /> The previously mentioned bit about (paraphrasing) &quot;How can my Sorcerer be more useful/whatever to &quot;x&quot; Demon?&quot; fails to note the *reason* WHY demons want sorcerers/whomever in the first place: the demon, itself, may be vastly more powerful than the sorcerer/human, but it's ability to act/function in the material world is often greatly curtailed/limited (as indicated in D:tF), and having sorcerers/humans/whatever to act through/for them, or provide them with Faith, is critical. Even a sorcerer with just a few dots spread among a couple Paths/Numina can provide the demon with a conduit/means of working itself into the broader world (especially if the other rules for demons, pre-D:tF, are used, wherein a demon can tempt/sway a sorcerer with the promise of greater power if said sorcerer serves it/enters into pacts with it). Devil's Due -- which, granted, is a Dark Ages book -- provides a *wonderful* alternative for how demons might bestow &quot;gifts&quot; to mortals -- sorcerers/mages included -- in exchange for service/pacts. Even if the ST wants to tweak the mechanics involved a bit, it still gives excellent insight into the underlying relationship/reasoning behind the demon/mortal interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Investments predate <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> and <b>Devil\u2019s Due</b>, and in fact make up a third kind of \u201cmagic for humans\u201d that coexists alongside Awakened Magick and Sorcery. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https: