\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">f rubber has volition and the ability to move, why doesn't glue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because my neoprene base has bonded instantly with his surface of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's quite nice, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T11:06:47-07:00","id":139561,"title":"","content":"I could use some glue right now; the frame of my glasses just snapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T15:45:59-07:00","id":146098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster#post126482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm playing a Sorcerer using Sorcerer Revised and I need some help. For you that don't know, let me state some things. Sorcerers are weak and need a lot of experience to be effective. They're super squishy, and are only able to cast good spells as long as they have temporary willpower. Firstly: This book is terribly written. I mean half the needed stuff for a Sorcerer isn't defined any where in the book and they have multiple words for a single concept, like number of successes. It took me multiple read throughs of the casting mechanics to understand them because they are so horribly written. Like holy crap, I'm still not sure if I'm throwing fireballs correctly. Secondly: This book is terribly written. I mean this as in, they literally took the Sorcerer's hand book, copy pasted it, spent a Saturday to update some stuff, and published it. There are things in this that don't even exist in the rest of the book. Like the Path of Cursing or Ephemera. Also you can do aggravated damage, but it doesn't say whether Path of Healing actually helps since it's for healing mortals, and mortals don't care about aggravated. Also some of the rolls don't make a lick of darn sense. Alchemy is Intelligence + Alchemy, but Advanced Chemistry is Intelligence + Science. It says you are normally using Attribute + Ability for a roll, yet I can't find an ability named Alchemy, but there is one for science, so do I use the Alchemy Path rating? Then there's Weathercontrol which uses Manipulation + Willpower for it, so you're getting a huge number of successes. So there's a bunch of Paths that ignore the go to rule already. But then there's the Path of Healing which uses Manipulation + Intuition. Intuition was removed in Revised IIRC, and is not even a choice on the sheet anymore. Ignoring why would you use Intuition over Medicine FOR A HEALING BASED POWER, why is this in here? Thirdly: Useless Paths are all over the place. Shadowcasting, Alchemy, and Enchanting are all terribly useless. Alchemy and Enchanting are ritual only paths, meaning you can't do them in combat really, which makes sense. However, they require a 3 experience point investment to learn a ritual, what this means is that you can have a single point spent into Enchanting, and can only make a single magical item that has super weak effects. Enchanting and Alchemy are suppose to be the Bread and Butter of a Sorcerer, yet he has to blow 30 experience to even bling himself out with basic stuff. Why would anyone ever touch this? Removing the ritual only part of this would make it so much better, yet it's effectively pointless to take at all since it's so costly. Finally: Spells are in general hard to cast. Want to throw a fireball? Enjoy your minimum 3 turns of casting time for that Aspect 3. If you don't get the 5 successes required to do your 1 lethal damage fireball, you need to spend another 3 turns casting. You could hang the spell and use it later but now you're doing 2 willpower per spell, so you can fire 5 spells that do super low damage. Hanging spells also makes any rolls involving social way harder because you're focusing, so you can be a prepared Sorcerer, or a social one. Well you could just spend mana to lower the difficulty, but that also makes the spell require something and you can only hold 5 mana at a time. Assuming you survive the 3 turns, you will actually be able to kill something by blowing a lot of your mana. You could avoid willpower by casting the spell at a lower level, but then you're not doing much of anything at all. Sure it's easier, but your spells aren't as good really compared to a shotgun and cast way slower still. You can also use willpower to cast faster but that raises the difficulty so you need more successes since you need 1 per aspect you want in your spell effectively doing nothing. So what's the point of being a Sorcerer if they're literally a 10 shot shotgun (assuming they maxed willpower). My question is how do you make a viable Sorcerer that can actually be useful, since a pistol seems better in all sense, and what houserules are basically required to make them actually some what good, because gods know they need it. I hope Sorcerer does get a new book after M20 because it's a lot of neat stuff like for psychics which are top tier amazing, but Sorcerers are way worse do to their super long cast times, and willpower limits. I'm playing a Sorcerer in an upcoming game so if anyone has any advice, please feel free to speak up.</div> </div> </div> </div> Who cares about throwing fire balls in combat when you can do so much amazing sorcery with the other paths. With summoning binding and warding you can turn demons into your pawns, with Fortune you can curse others and give yourself the luck needed to win a fortune of wealth, with divination you can know what the future holds and with shapehsifting you can look like anyone you wish. Think about what you would do in the world if you had this sort of power, think about how influential you could become. Sorcerer's are like gods among insects, though perhaps, not among demons. As a rule focused piece of advice there's a line somewhere which states that you don't need to buy rituals for ritual only paths like alchemy and enchantment which are actually *very* powerful. I would add that you can also be a psychic who learned sorcery as per the merrit in the revised edition and that Dream Speakers revised (while also showcasing new paths) supports the Path + Attribute system which is mentioned as a new standard and one worth converting to for a variety of sensible reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T15:55:47-07:00","id":146130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=135087#post135087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's any of this have to do with Sorcerer?</div> </div> </div> </div> Good question, I tried to bring the conversation back to its original topic but hey maybe I'm full of shit in my post because I was high on glue from smelling Thebian and Mord, I guess I just couldn't resist sniffing at two people who were stuck together in an onyx path forum :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T02:28:59-07:00","id":147739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=146098#post146098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Who cares about throwing fire balls in combat when you can do so much amazing sorcery with the other paths. With summoning binding and warding you can turn demons into your pawns, with Fortune you can curse others and give yourself the luck needed to win a fortune of wealth, with divination you can know what the future holds and with shapehsifting you can look like anyone you wish. Think about what you would do in the world if you had this sort of power, think about how influential you could become. Sorcerer's are like gods among insects, though perhaps, not among demons. As a rule focused piece of advice there's a line somewhere which states that you don't need to buy rituals for ritual only paths like alchemy and enchantment which are actually *very* powerful. I would add that you can also be a psychic who learned sorcery as per the merrit in the revised edition and that Dream Speakers revised (while also showcasing new paths) supports the Path + Attribute system which is mentioned as a new standard and one worth converting to for a variety of sensible reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You posted this from an iPad, didn\u2019t you? <br /> <br /> I had overlooked <b>Dreamspeakers</b>\u2019 additions to hedge magic. Thanks for the reminder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T01:19:03-07:00","id":148524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=147739#post147739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You posted this from an iPad, didn\u2019t you? I had overlooked <b>Dreamspeakers</b>\u2019 additions to hedge magic. Thanks for the reminder.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not from an iPad, I used a shitty tablet and yes I'm aware I can't hit the enter/return key to put spaces between paragraphs with this but hey I'm in India and I'm traveling with no phone and no laptop so it is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T01:27:11-07:00","id":148530,"title":"","content":"Outlander I'm not sure if you known this but dataweaver has made some modifications to sorcerery which your storyteller might just be willing to learn and incorporate (if time is available and the inclination is there). I have done the same myself and *really* made sorcerery a powerful force, I used it in a game I set in the mythic ages where magic was a fair bit different, basically I used the same rules as presented in dark ages mage but switched out the pillars for paths and made the second dot in a path the first dot (which then made the sixth dot as presented in the book the fifth dot in this game) plus we made the whole system a bit more free form. This is only a solution for a fairly dedicated group in which all the players know the rules and can get into it, not a real suggestion for you (sorry), just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T01:35:15-07:00","id":148532,"title":"","content":"One last thing outlander, if you're playing In a demon the fallen game then I would advise your storyteller to let you have at least ten dots of sorcery and an equal number of dots as demons in all relevant fields (ie attributes, abilities etc) I'd go with alchemy or enchantment, summoning binding and warding and maybe healing (just to save your own ass) if you want to play a power broker of sorts (though one who better hang back in combat), alchemy and enchantment give you a lot of bargaining power, there's nothing like selling magic items to demons to make you feel like one bad ass merchant of death! lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T01:36:00-07:00","id":148533,"title":"","content":"Not a complaint; just an observation. I do most of my posting from an iPad; but while I\u2019ve resolved the paragraphs problem, I have to jump through some inconvenient hoops to do so. So I sympathize with your plight. <br /> <br /> Back on topic: I like that the Shamanic Paths are more varied in the Attributes they use; in particular, the use of Social Attributes for Paths that involve interacting with entities is very welcome. I wouldn\u2019t mind a Path or two that\u2019s based on Perception, for instance. <br /> <br /> But I\u2019d rather have an Ability in the pool than the Path rating, considering that M20 will be explicitly tying Abilities to specific magical styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T02:41:16-07:00","id":148551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=148533#post148533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a complaint; just an observation. I do most of my posting from an iPad; but while I\u2019ve resolved the paragraphs problem, I have to jump through some inconvenient hoops to do so. So I sympathize with your plight. Back on topic: I like that the Shamanic Paths are more varied in the Attributes they use; in particular, the use of Social Attributes for Paths that involve interacting with entities is very welcome. I wouldn\u2019t mind a Path or two that\u2019s based on Perception, for instance. But I\u2019d rather have an Ability in the pool than the Path rating, considering that M20 will be explicitly tying Abilities to specific magical styles.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see your point on tying abilities with magic but in the case of sorcerey i have to disagree, when you're forced to roll using an ability that you don't even have and that your character would never have according to your artistic vision of the character then you're hamstrung; also I would add that how skilled you are with your path should be directly relevant regarding your dice rolls. I support tying abilities to magical styles and am looking forward to seeing what M20 includes in this regard but when it comes down to being a deciding factor in a two characteristic dice pool I just can't go for it, the ability rolled on should be the path in my opinion. I also support sorcerers optionally having a magical attribute similar to Foundation in Dark Ages (which can be somewhat burdensome in terms of experience and freebie points), the key word here being optionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T07:50:35-07:00","id":148696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=148551#post148551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see your point on tying abilities with magic but in the case of sorcerey i have to disagree, when you're forced to roll using an ability that you don't even have and that your character would never have according to your artistic vision of the character then you're hamstrung;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a concern the way I\u2019m thinking of doing it: instead of the Ability being determined solely by the Path, I\u2019m figuring that it would be \u201chere\u2019s a set of seven or eight Abilities that could be appropriate to this Path; compare this set to the set of Abilities featured in the Practice you chose to follow, and pick one that matches both. If there\u2019s no overlap, talk it over with your Storyteller and pick one of your Practice\u2019s associated Abilities.\u201d<br /> <br /> In short, Ability should be determined primarily by Practice, and Practice had <i>better</i> align with your artistic vision of the character or you\u2019re not doing it right \u2014 and I never say that lightly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=148551#post148551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also I would add that how skilled you are with your path should be directly relevant regarding your dice rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see a need for this, as long as your rating in the Path determines what you can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T08:34:36-07:00","id":148717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=148696#post148696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a concern the way I\u2019m thinking of doing it: instead of the Ability being determined solely by the Path, I\u2019m figuring that it would be \u201chere\u2019s a set of seven or eight Abilities that could be appropriate to this Path; compare this set to the set of Abilities featured in the Practice you chose to follow, and pick one that matches both. If there\u2019s no overlap, talk it over with your Storyteller and pick one of your Practice\u2019s associated Abilities.\u201d In short, Ability should be determined primarily by Practice, and Practice had <i>better</i> align with your artistic vision of the character or you\u2019re not doing it right \u2014 and I never say that lightly. I don\u2019t see a need for this, as long as your rating in the Path determines what you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see your point with the various abilities you can choose for use in sorcerery dice pools but I still prefer to say ''if you mastered that path then you roll five dice for it, not three or two or even four because that's what you have in a relevant ability, if you're using the path then you're rolling with the path because it represents how skilled you are with that path, not an ability that is separate from it''. That being said I do see your point and feel that it's a good one, I guess our differing preferences come down to just that. After seeing Dream Speakers revised use paths instead of relevant abilities in the dice pool, I went with it because it felt right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T16:40:47-07:00","id":1403433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=126537#post126537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s little chance of an M20 Sorcerer any time soon, unfortunately; but once M20 comes out, I intend to tackle this issue. A preliminary thought I\u2019ve had is that M20\u2019s new Focus rules assign common Abilities to the Style as well as common tools: for M20 Sorcerer, the Attribute + Ability pool for a given Path should be dependent on the sorcerer\u2019s Style. As an extreme example, a sorcerer who\u2019s Style involves bargaining with supernatural forces might use a social attribute such as Charisma rather than Intelligence when forming his dice pool, and/or an Ability such as Etiquette or Performance instead of Occult.<br /> <br /> In terms of house rules: consider dropping most of the Willpower costs; the casting times are more than adequate to prevent the sorcerer from spamming their rituals; and consider allowing the use of mana in place of Willpower in those cases that still have a cost. Consider removing the effects of Aspects from the Difficulty and Time determination; the fact that you must allocate successes already implies increased chance of failure and a longer casting time due to the need to accumulate more successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dataweaver did you ever do anything else with this? It looks great<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T13:37:59-07:00","id":1404082,"title":"","content":"Oh man it's been years since we touched this thread. I believe Dataweaver went on to make this thread:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\"> Updating and Expanding Sorcerer - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The purpose of this thread is to explore ways to take the Hedge Magic system and bring it fully into the x20 era. Full disclosure: I'm posting this in the Classic World of Darkness forum instead of the Mage forum because I prefer to treat Hedge Magic as something distinct from the metaphysics of Mage: the </div> </div> </div><br /> Even then, this is three years out of date.<br /> <br /> Ironically, I'm pretty close to finishing my sorcerer rules due to the whole Covid thing. I'm like 90% done with the magic rules. Rest is just fluff and chargen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T02:37:32-07:00","id":1404209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=1404082#post1404082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man it's been years since we touched this thread. I believe Dataweaver went on to make this thread:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\"> Updating and Expanding Sorcerer - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The purpose of this thread is to explore ways to take the Hedge Magic system and bring it fully into the x20 era. Full disclosure: I'm posting this in the Classic World of Darkness forum instead of the Mage forum because I prefer to treat Hedge Magic as something distinct from the metaphysics of Mage: the </div> </div> </div><br /> Even then, this is three years out of date.<br /> <br /> Ironically, I'm pretty close to finishing my sorcerer rules due to the whole Covid thing. I'm like 90% done with the magic rules. Rest is just fluff and chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I woulddefinitely be interested in seeing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T03:55:55-07:00","id":1404215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=126537#post126537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s little chance of an M20 Sorcerer any time soon, unfortunately; but once M20 comes out, I intend to tackle this issue. A preliminary thought I\u2019ve had is that M20\u2019s new Focus rules assign common Abilities to the Style as well as common tools: for M20 Sorcerer, the Attribute + Ability pool for a given Path should be dependent on the sorcerer\u2019s Style. As an extreme example, a sorcerer who\u2019s Style involves bargaining with supernatural forces might use a social attribute such as Charisma rather than Intelligence when forming his dice pool, and/or an Ability such as Etiquette or Performance instead of Occult.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can there be an Appearance or Strength-based Sorcerer in your system? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> A Dexterity or Wits-based Sorcery sounds even more unlikely, but at the same time it makes one wonder...Certainly Charisma and Stamina do fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T08:03:01-07:00","id":1404240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=1404215#post1404215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be an Appearance or Strength-based Sorcerer in your system? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> A Dexterity or Wits-based Sorcery sounds even more unlikely, but at the same time it makes one wonder...Certainly Charisma and Stamina do fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. If you can justify a Strength+Skill pool, you can justify a Strength+Ability pool for a Path; you just need the right Focus. For instance, Strength+Athletics is used frequently; a Sorcerer whose Practice is Martial Arts could use that as a dice pool for, say, Hellfire: think Street Fighter. Appearance+Expression could use the Practice of Bardism (<b>Book of Secrets</b>) for Fascination.<br /> <br /> Upon reflection, I wouldn't try to the an Attribute to the Paradigm after all; the choice of Attribute should be made in terms of how the Ability gets used, as normal.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I could also see the Art of Desire using a lot of Attributes, including Strength and Appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-23-2020, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T16:40:37-07:00","id":1404319,"title":"","content":"I made a now forgotten attempt at try to re balance sorcerer and other human caster rules a few years ago here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-for-sorcerers</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps, I kinda hate how white-wolf had a habit of taking their more obscure game-lines out behind the shed. Sorcerer, strike force 0, mummy, KotE, and others all had a lot of potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T17:43:22-07:00","id":1404325,"title":"","content":"Heres all you need. Its kind of awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/259124.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"> Sorcerer's Companion - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sorcerer's Companion - The Sorcerer's Companion provides new options for Players and advice for Storytellers of Sorcerer games utilizing Sorcer </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T19:27:15-07:00","id":1404339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/126482-sorcerer-a-better-class-of-caster?p=1404319#post1404319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a now forgotten attempt at try to re balance sorcerer and other human caster rules a few years ago here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1240551-better-rules-for-sorcerers\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-for-sorcerers</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps, I kinda hate how white-wolf had a habit of taking their more obscure game-lines out behind the shed. Sorcerer, strike force 0, mummy, KotE, and others all had a lot of potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never even heard of Strike Force 0.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East and Mummy weren't as